node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
.turbo
**/.turbo
.git
assets-src
test/fixtures/pack-src
packages/client/public/assets/tilesets/pack
packages/client/public/assets/sprites/pack
packages/client/public/assets/baked
# The frozen legacy pipeline (scripts/capture-golden-baseline.mjs) still
# writes REAL licensed pixels straight from assets-src/ to these vendor-named
# paths (see .gitignore) — gitignored, so `git archive` never ships them, but
# a Docker build context reads the working tree directly. Verified: without
# this rule a stray `npm run golden:capture` residue on disk gets COPIed
# straight into the image (I-12).
packages/client/public/assets/tilesets/limezu
packages/client/public/assets/sprites/limezu
packages/client/public/assets/ui/limezu
# Contact sheets (npm run contact) — Task 3's pack-QA review artifact, real
# licensed pixel crops rendered straight off assets-src/. Gitignored, but
# docker-compose's agent-bake service builds Dockerfile.client's
# intermediate `build` stage (target: build) and keeps it as a runnable,
# taggable image — COPY . . before this rule existed pulled contact/ into
# that image on every build, fixture or real (I-12).
contact
# Per-cell pack inventory (npm run pack:index) — sources/limezu.index.json is
# 826 MB of hashes/palettes derived from the real pack. Gitignored (mirrors
# .gitignore's sources/*.index.json exactly); excluding it here keeps every
# build context small and keeps derived-from-licensed-art fingerprints out of
# the same intermediate stage as above.
sources/*.index.json
# Self-host secrets and data (Plan 6 final review, Important finding 1):
# root-only patterns (no leading **/) match ONLY at the build-context root —
# this file's own node_modules/.turbo rules already knew that (paired with
# **/node_modules, **/.turbo above), but *.db*/.env* were left root-only.
# Verified: without the **/ forms, packages/server/.env and
# packages/server/botville.db entered the agent-bake build-stage image
# byte-for-byte. DEPLOY.md tells self-host operators to put real secrets in
# exactly that .env, so this is a production-credentials leak, not just a
# hygiene one.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
# User-authored agent roster (docker-compose.yml's agent-bake --roster) — a
# real one is COPY . .'d into the same build stage for nothing; the running
# container already reads it via a runtime bind mount (Minor finding 2, same
# class as the above).
roster/*.json
